entary row operations:\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}=\\frac{1}{1+2\\text{i}}{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{2}={R}_{2}+(2\\text{i}-3){R}_{1}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's apply the row operations to $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1+2\\text{i} & -2-4\\text{i} \\\\ 3-2\\text{i} & \\text{i}\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{1+2\\text{i}}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 3-2\\text{i} & \\text{i}\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(2\\text{i}-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 6-3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the result is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 6-3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-140381/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef2e7753-83f4-5826-a04f-89616d34c578"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-140381"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
